            </note>
            <note corresp="#d812-f2" n="7" xml:id="d812-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1928v02#pg_816">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>,
                        pp. 816</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d812-f3" n="8" xml:id="d812-f3-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning treaties with Denmark, Germany, and Great Britain,
                    see <ref target="frus1928v02#pg_718">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>,
                        pp. 718</ref> ff., <ref target="frus1928v02#pg_862">pp. 862</ref> ff., and
                        <ref target="frus1928v02#pg_943">pp. 943</ref> ff.; for that with Italy,
                    Japan, the Netherlands, and Spain, see <ref target="frus1928v03#pg_102">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 102</ref> ff., <ref
                        target="frus1928v03#pg_135">pp. 135</ref> ff., <ref
                        target="frus1928v03#pg_142">pp. 412</ref> ff., and <ref
                        target="frus1928v03#pg_879">pp. 879</ref> ff. The treaties with Hungary,
                    Norway, and Portugal were concluded in 1929.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d812-f4" n="9" xml:id="d812-f4-content">
                <p>For the Bryan treaties for the advancement of general peace, see <ref
                        target="frus1914#pg_1130"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1914, index, p. 1130</ref>; <ref target="frus1915#pg_1328">1915, index,
                        1328</ref>; and <ref target="frus1916#pg_1007">1916, index, p.
                    1007</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d812-f5" n="10" xml:id="d812-f5-content">
                <p>Drafts not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
